<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taula de Canvi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1401</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Taula de Canvi de Barcelona</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Taula de Canvi ('exchange table') of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> was a public bank founded by the city council in 1401 to hold deposits, make payments and manage the city's debt. One of the first public banks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, it lasted in various forms until the nineteenth century.</p></div>
